    delta: 155796 counts in 596.0 ms -> 66.9188 MHz
    delta: 156601 counts in 591.2 ms -> 67.8122 MHz
    delta: 157903 counts in 599.7 ms -> 67.4016 MHz
    delta: 154827 counts in 591.5 ms -> 67.0111 MHz
    delta: 156696 counts in 594.7 ms -> 67.4512 MHz
    delta: 156053 counts in 617.8 ms -> 64.6653 MHz
  --- SUMMARY ---
    CFGMCLK frequency: mean 66.8457 MHz, median 67.0111 MHz, stdev 1.0078 MHz, n=9
    min 64.6653 MHz, max 67.8190 MHz

  Two independent CFGMCLK measurements on the same board and the same session:
    run 1: mean 67.1583 MHz, median 67.3927, stdev 1.3325, n=9
    run 2: mean 66.8457 MHz, median 67.0111, stdev 1.0078, n=9
  They agree to within 0.5%.

CONCLUSION. The fabric ring oscillator does not oscillate on this AX7203. This is CONFIRMED,
not inferred: the identical probe, differing only in the clock source, counts correctly at
~67 MHz on CFGMCLK and never advances on the ring oscillator, over 30 reads and 15 seconds.

CORROBORATION. The parent repository's fpga/HARDWARE_SSOT.md and docs/fpga/clocking.md state:
  "Ring Oscillator (DOES NOT WORK) ... -abc9 inserts SCC breaker that destroys the
   combinational loop - Behavioral assign osc = ~osc is optimized away by Yosys - LUT1
   primitive instantiation also broken by ABC9 SCC detection"
  and that the board has NO working external oscillator, so CFGMCLK is the only working clock.
